From: local private research
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi_osal: Use timer_delete_sync() on Linux 6.16+

v6.16 removed the del_timer_sync() wrapper (commit "timers: Remove
del_timer_sync()"), keeping only timer_delete_sync(). With 6.18 the call
is no longer declared anywhere, so GCC 14 reports:

  mt_osal_timer.c:98:31: error: implicit declaration of function
  'del_timer_sync'; did you mean 'dev_mc_sync'?
  [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Keep the old name behind a version gate: both functions are identical,
the rename happened in 6.16.

Signed-off-by: local private research
---
--- a/mt_osal_timer.c
+++ b/mt_osal_timer.c
@@ -94,10 +94,16 @@
 	OS_TIMER *pTimer,
 	unsigned char *pCancelled)
 {
-	if (timer_pending(pTimer))
-		*pCancelled = del_timer_sync(pTimer);
-	else
+	if (!timer_pending(pTimer)) {
 		*pCancelled = true;
+		return;
+	}
+
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+	*pCancelled = timer_delete_sync(pTimer);
+#else
+	*pCancelled = del_timer_sync(pTimer);
+#endif
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(mt_os_del_timer);
 
